  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nA = (9 / 16) ÷ (25 / 36)\n\nB = 9 ÷ [(16 ÷ 25) ÷ 36]\n\nC = [9 ÷ (16 ÷ 25)] ÷ 36\n\nD = (9 ÷ 16) ÷ (25 ÷ 36)\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nTo divide fractions: (a / b) ÷ (c / d) = (a / b) × (d / c)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n**A:**\n\nA = (9 / 16) ÷ (25 / 36)\n\nA = (9 / 16) × (36 / 25)\n\nA = (9 × 36) / (16 × 25)\n\nA = 324 / 400\n\nA = 81 / 100\n\n**B:**\n\nB = 9 ÷ [(16 ÷ 25) ÷ 36]\n\nCalculate inside the brackets first:\n\n16 ÷ 25 = 0.64\n\n0.64 ÷ 36 = 0.0177778\n\nB = 9 ÷ 0.0177778\n\nB = 506.25\n\n**C:**\n\nC = [9 ÷ (16 ÷ 25)] ÷ 36\n\nCalculate inside the brackets first:\n\n16 ÷ 25 = 0.64\n\n9 ÷ 0.64 = 14.0625\n\nC = 14.0625 ÷ 36\n\nC = 0.390625\n\n**D:**\n\nD = (9 ÷ 16) ÷ (25 ÷ 36)\n\nD = (9 / 16) × (36 / 25)\n\nD = (9 × 36) / (16 × 25)\n\nD = 324 / 400\n\nD = 81 / 100\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nA = D = 81 / 100\n\nB = 506.25\n\nC = 0.390625\n\n**A and D are equal. B and C are different. So A and D are true and equal, while B and C are not equal.**",
